  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Three points have coordinates $A(1,2)$, $B(3,10)$ and $C(p,8)$. Find the values of $p$ if:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A$, $B$ and $C$ are collinear",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=\\frac{5}{2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{10-2}{3-1}\\\\m_{AB}&=4\\end{align*}$$\nCollinear points have the same gradient along their common line.\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{AC}&=\\frac{8-2}{p-1}\\\\m_{AC}&=\\frac{6}{p-1}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6}{p-1}&=4\\\\6&=4(p-1)\\\\6&=4p-4\\\\10&=4p\\\\p&=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$AC$ is perpendicular to $AB$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=-23$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{10-2}{3-1}\\\\m_{AB}&=4\\end{align*}$$\nPerpendicular gradients have product $-1$, so $m_{AC}=-\\frac{1}{4}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{AC}&=\\frac{8-2}{p-1}\\\\m_{AC}&=\\frac{6}{p-1}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6}{p-1}&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\24&=-(p-1)\\\\24&=-p+1\\\\p&=-23\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
